    "created_at": "2023-11-13T12:17:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-11-13T12:17:22Z",
    "body": "> Looks like some implementations to convert this ToString ([Firefox](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/source/js/src/vm/StructuredClone.cpp#1846), [Safari](https://searchfox.org/wubkat/source/Source/WebCore/bindings/js/SerializedScriptValue.cpp#1603)), so I think this is a worthwhile addition.\r\n\r\nThe Firefox code you linked isn't using the ES-262 [`ToString`](https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-tostring) method. We actually check for primitive strings in the `if` [one line above](https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/fe8b30e982c86d26ccf1f14d825c0de870b91f27/js/src/vm/StructuredClone.cpp#1845). So for everything that isn't a primitive string we always fall back to `\"Error\"`.",
